{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"492423553055931673f361b6fb74533c2b6010547bab018285d416851d581bb9","digest":{"component_or_area":"DC adapter pagination structural guard","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_base.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py","test_no_search_issues_call_relies_on_the_default_page_size","_search_issues_calls_taking_the_default","search_issues","_TRANSPORT_SRC","commit 4213081d23"],"problem_keywords":["structural guard","vacuous test","AST scan","module split","pagination","search_issues","rot"],"propositions":["The pagination guard scans only transport.py, but commit 465d moved all search_issues() calls out of transport.py into _base.py and _issues.py, causing the AST guard to find zero call sites and pass unconditionally.","The guard must be widened to scan every *.py in adapters/jira_datacenter/ and must include a non-vacuity assertion that fails if no search_issues calls are found, preventing future rot.","A teeth test must prove the widened guard detects uncapped search_issues calls attributed to non-transport modules (specifically _base.py and _issues.py).","Four sibling structural guards in the test suite were also emptied by module splits and are now vacuous; these require separate fixes per guard as each is a reviewable unit."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787425632066922001,"uuid":"6cf163a3-7961-40ef-85e4-6e96ceb89379"}